# 30_splitfield_lucid_RGB.ledc — Split-Field Lucid, RGB inner/outer build
# RGB variant of 30_splitfield_lucid. Audio + speech IDENTICAL (6 Hz isochronic dream bed).
# Split-field per eye — LEFT eye (mask 3) at 16 Hz, RIGHT eye (mask 12) at 6 Hz — which is
# exactly how this build's rings group (mask 3 = inner-left+outer-left, mask 12 =
# inner-right+outer-right). RGB adds a DICHOPTIC COLOUR split: the alert 16 Hz left eye is
# cool blue (32,96,255), the dreamy 6 Hz right eye warm amber (255,160,32).
# SAFETY: the LEFT 16 Hz sits in the 15-25 Hz band, so it is kept DIM (<=18%) and SINGLE-EYE
# (never full-field bright) — the validator WARNs on those rows BY DESIGN. Ends dark. See base.
#
# LED: time freq duty bright R G B mask [env phase]

# --- Induction: BOTH eyes 10 Hz alpha, dim cool-white, fade in ---
0 10 50 >0 180 200 255 15 1 0       # both eyes (mask 15) 10 Hz sine, fade-in
A 0 200 0 >0 6 1                   # isochronic 6 Hz theta dream bed; vol fade-in
S 3000 default 47 "Eyes closed, body still. Let a calm alpha rhythm settle you."
15000 10 50 18 180 200 255 15 1 0   # brightness 18% (dim)
A 60000 200 0 90 6 1               # audio bed settled

# --- Split field: LEFT 16 Hz (blue, alert) / RIGHT 6 Hz (amber, dream) ---
120000 16 50 18 32 96 255 3 1 0     # LEFT eye (mask 3): 16 Hz alert cue, cool blue (danger-band warn expected)
120000 6 50 18 255 160 32 12 1 0    # RIGHT eye (mask 12): 6 Hz theta/dream, warm amber
S 120000 default 47 "One eye quickens, one eye slows. Stay aware as you drift into the dream."
S 420000 default 47 "If you notice you are dreaming, stay calm and steady. You are lucid."

# --- Soft Off: both eyes + audio fade to dark (no wake-up) ---
720000 16 50 >18 32 96 255 3 1 0    # LEFT brightness ramp-out
720000 6 50 >18 255 160 32 12 1 0   # RIGHT brightness ramp-out
A 720000 200 0 >90 6 1             # audio bed fade
S 720000 default 47 "Letting the light fade now. Rest, or dream on."
900000 16 50 0 32 96 255 3 1 0      # LEFT -> 0
900000 6 50 0 255 160 32 12 1 0     # RIGHT -> 0
A 900000 200 0 0 6 1               # audio -> 0
